993 and add the service account (card reopened); 100576 which of the final 15 questions came from the meta-audit (card 196); 191 tag desktop clients after 1000490; 1000480 QNFO/.github release pipeline may need a token with workflows scope; 1000275 six wedged workflow runs (GitHub answers 403 and 409; card 172 was closed at birth, GitHub Support or the owner); 100168 apply the main-gate ruleset (design choice between direct pushes by 16 workflows and moving status commits off main); 2805 write lock on the owner machine for sync_system_prompt.py; Postmaster registration (card bp26-postmaster-registration). (7) Cost: monthly_cost_run_rate_usd 1467 has a 777 USD floor (owner clients 322, direct providers 450, plan 5) and the Workers AI window still holds the 10-18 to 10-21 burst until about 11-17; workers_ai_cost_30d_usd 300 vs 95; worker_count 35 vs 30 (qnfo-workers stub is recreated by a Workers Builds trigger, issue 1000156; voice-stt owner decision; folds of qnfo-evolve and qnfo-model-eval need a session); no cap or target was changed; watch q08_human_reads_7d (1407 vs floor 50) after the q08 budget cut. (8) Time-gated: ROOT-CAUSE tickets 1000301 to 1000310 earliest pass 2026-10-27 07:37Z; tick metrics clear 10-27 03:00Z to 06:10Z; false_stops_7d 10-27 11:00Z and 10-29; ops_agent_empty_answers_7d 10-31; 100419 from 10-28 09:08Z; 100299 daily reads from 11-02; 2008 on 11-08; 2722 and 100190 learner and attention windows 10-27 and 10-28. (9) Interim q08 daily research desk runs as a scheduled task of a Claude session, which NO-CLAUDE-RUNTIME-DEPENDENCY-1 forbids (flagged by rem-a7, not removed): replace it with a worker cron. (10) 100459 side effects: IDENTITY-BOUND cards are now held, so human_wait_oldest_min can trip; cards closed at birth since 2026-10-12 (ids 125, 172, 173, 174, 175, 189) stay closed by the owner default-approve directive. (11) 16 BP26 metrics now measure real gaps (see summary): the program managers own them; 1000344 retention purge (886 rows past retention, 683 mail bodies) is approved and not implemented (issue 1000481).',
